{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Binding repair completed with fail-closed guards. Before mutation, bridge fsck had no unknown event types, no store-integrity findings, no would_terminal/local_gone/retired_overlap/dangling findings, and exactly unbound_jira={REB-806, REB-807, REB-808}; 1,135 absent_in_window_unprobed entries remained non-alerting and untouched. ACLI re-read immediately before repair proved all three Jira issues are Done and exactly match their local code_review artifacts by summary, description/revision/PASS fingerprint, and sole rebar-id label. Under rebar._store.lock.write_lock, BindingStore confirmed each forward/reverse slot was empty, bind_confirm restored a750-2710-e903-4a45<->REB-806, d494-d34f-cf36-43df<->REB-807, and ee21-fcd3-edad-462c<->REB-808, then save persisted atomically. commit_and_push_tickets_branch(strict=True) delivered tracker commit adadb8966f287495b806f154e227d3736ca4a292. Post-reload queries proved all six forward/reverse lookups. Post-repair bridge fsck: unknown_event_types=[], all alerting binding-drift buckets including unbound_jira=[], store_integrity=[]; the non-alerting unprobed baseline remained 1,135. No ticket or Jira issue was created, archived, or transitioned."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786907738635739001,"uuid":"58275974-65ab-400d-8b3a-23bec8139af9"}